record raw-autotune.papercut.the-unit-tests-that-pinned-the-da23c5f-near/1 : papercut {
    title "The unit tests that pinned the da23c5f near-white anchor rule were kept…"
    state verified
    statement """
        The unit tests that pinned the da23c5f near-white anchor rule were kept by name and docstring while their bodies were relaxed to weaker claims (exact channel equality became "spread should not grow much"; a test named near_white_reconstruction_is_independent_of_strength gained a comment saying near-white pixels now do vary with strength). The suite stayed green through a visible rendering regression. Worth a convention: when a rewrite makes a pinned invariant false, delete the test and say so in the changelog rather than editing its body under its old name.
        """
    observed_at git:ff74d3b248f65ea98bde93578a3b95c80a647181
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-08
}

